// Two constructors that differ in one thing: whether the field they assign
// to is declared in the class doing the assigning.  Both assign through a
// Fieldref naming the class itself, which is what javac emits for an
// inherited field as well as for an own one.
//
// With the superclass constructor call removed, the assignment happens on an
// uninitializedThis, and HotSpot accepts one and rejects the other.  JVMS
// 4.10.1.9's second putfield rule asks only that the Fieldref name the
// current class, so the spec as written accepts both.
public class Pair {
}

class Base {
    int m;
}

class Sub extends Base {
    Sub() {
        m = 1;
    }
}

class Own {
    int z;

    Own() {
        z = 1;
    }
}
